    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Without loss of generality we may assume that $\calX $ is minimal. Let $f^{\ast }$ be a left adjoint to $f_{\ast }$. Choose a regular cardinal $\kappa $ large enough that the composition 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  \calC \stackrel{j_{\calC }}{\rightarrow } \calP (\calC ) \stackrel{f^{\ast }}{\rightarrow } \calX  \]
</div>
    <p>
       carries each object $C \in \calC $ to a $\kappa $-compact object of $\calX $. Enlarging $\kappa $ if necessary, we may assume that $\calX $ is $\kappa $-accessible and that the collection of $\kappa $-compact objects is stable under finite limits (Proposition <a href="/tag/1FDDC5" data-tag="1FDDC5">5.4.7.4</a>). Let $\calD $ be the collection of $\kappa $-compact objects of $\calX $. The proof of Proposition <a href="/tag/075DA7" data-tag="075DA7">6.1.5.3</a> shows that the inclusion $\calD \subseteq \calX $ can be extended to a left exact localization functor ${f'}^{\ast }: \calP (\calD ) \rightarrow \calX $. 
    <p>
      Using Theorem <a href="/tag/9EF11D" data-tag="9EF11D">5.1.5.6</a>, we conclude that the composition $j_{\calD } \circ f^{\ast } \circ j_{\calC }: \calC \rightarrow \calP (\calD )$ can be extended to a colimit-preserving functor ${f''}^{\ast }: \calP (\calC ) \rightarrow \calP (\calD )$, and that ${f'}^{\ast } \circ {f''}^{\ast }$ is homotopic to $f^{\ast }$. Proposition <a href="/tag/A529FA" data-tag="A529FA">6.1.5.2</a> implies that ${f''}^{\ast }$ is left exact. It follows that ${f'}^{\ast }$ and ${f''}^{\ast }$ admit right adjoints $f'_{\ast }$ and $f''_{\ast }$ with the desired properties. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
